  "fidelity": {
    "models": [
      "scikit-rf 2.2.0: ABCD cascade of 56 constant-k LC sections per line (L 120 uH + DCR 3.3 ohm, Cp 19.4 pF from SRF 3.3 MHz, Rp from Q=10; C 120 pF), Rs/Rl 1000 ohm, input RC 482 kHz (edge 726 ns), tap buffers GBW 10 MHz",
      "ladder responses -> impulse responses at the S/H instants by direct inverse DFT; FIR engine of tier R (rf.fir_apply)",
      "crossbar 10 kohm +-1 %, DNP-pad leakage, summer pole and R_f error, tanh with V_BE mismatch 2 mV and temperature, diff-amp gain error, track-and-hold acquisition error and phase error",
      "inter-line mutual inductance k (dipole estimate, alternating layout, 3 mm pitch), ribbon 30 pF/m + NEXT",
      "clock calibrated on tile-1 line 0, residual error 0.5 %; stage noise from params.json summer_noise; 12-bit DAC/ADC",
      "nominal metrics: nominal parts on the FULL test set of 4000; sweeps on a fixed stratified subset of 1000 examples (tolerance axes: mean of 4 boards); Monte Carlo 1000 trials on 800 examples"
    ],
    "omits": [
      "LUMPED-ELEMENT circuit model at ~1 MBd: NOT RF (wavelength >> board); no EM/layout/field solving, no hardware measurement",
      "inductor Q is only known as a datasheet minimum (>= 10 @ 796 kHz); Q = 30 is an assumed typical; Rp frequency independent; no inductor tempco or saturation",
      "mutual inductance is a dipole estimate between equal sections of neighbour lines (no capacitive/ground-return coupling); tolerance enters first order on top of the coupled nominal ladder",
      "op-amps are single-pole (GBW 10 MHz) with no slew limit, offset or output impedance beyond the ribbon driver (50 ohm assumed); diff pair is ideal tanh + V_BE offset (no beta, Early, emitter-tail variation)",
      "no clock jitter (static phase/period error only), no supply noise, no ground bounce, no temperature dependence except V_T",
      "tolerances are uniform within +-tol (a bounded distribution), independent per part with a shared tile-level component"
    ]
  },
